{"schema_version":1,"dataset_id":"metro-gap-clusters","country":"LK","source_ids":["metro-coverage","lk-metro","osm-walk-colombo","lk-census-2024","gig-data-gnd-boundaries","osm","overture-places"],"vintage":"Walk graph 2026-10 · Census 2024 · CM stops 2026-08 · Overture 2026-09-23.1","title":"Dense neighbourhoods beyond Metro Bus walking reach","description":"Contiguous groups of dense GN divisions where fewer than one in ten residents live within a 10-minute walk of a Colombo Metro Bus stop.","grain":"One row per gap cluster of adjacent study-area GN divisions with at least 15,000 residents beyond a 10-minute walk.","notes":["Derived by developing-country.org with scripts/build-metro-alternatives.mjs on the same model as the metro coverage tables: 80 m/min walking on the OpenStreetMap foot network (5 min = 400 m, 10 min = 800 m), reached streets buffered 50 m, a 5 m equal-area raster, Census 2024 GN population spread evenly within each division, Overture Maps office listings and OSM schools and hospitals.","Tier 1 divisions have at least 10,000 residents per km² (about the densest fifth of study-area divisions) and less than 10% of their area within a 10-minute walk of a stop. Tier 2 lowers density to 5,000/km², about the study-area median, and keeps only clusters with no tier-1 division, so suburban gaps the dense tier misses are shown without merging into the inner-city clusters.","Divisions belong to one cluster when their gig-data polygons share a boundary (at least 2 vertices within 25 m of the neighbour's outline). Only clusters with at least 15,000 residents beyond a 10-minute walk are kept.","The label point is the member division centroid nearest the population-weighted centre; walk_m_to_stop is the network walk from it to the nearest CM stop. The cluster outline in metro-gap-clusters.geojson is the dissolved division raster, simplified to 10 m."],"caveats":["Coverage-only analysis: no travel demand, origin–destination data, road capacity, bus operations, terminal space or cost is considered.","Population is spread evenly within each GN division; residents only, no workplace or daytime population; offices are listings, not jobs.","OSM street and path completeness limits every walkshed; candidate routes follow mapped main roads only."],"primary_key":["cluster_id"],"fields":[{"id":"cluster_id","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Cluster ID"},{"id":"name","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Cluster"},{"id":"tier","role":"dimension","type":"integer","label":"Density tier (1 = ≥ 10,000/km², 2 = ≥ 5,000/km²)"},{"id":"dsd","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"Main Divisional Secretariat division"},{"id":"gnd_count","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"GN divisions","unit":"divisions","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"gnd_ids","role":"dimension","type":"string","label":"GN division IDs"},{"id":"residents","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Residents","unit":"people","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"unserved_residents","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Residents beyond a 10-minute walk","unit":"people","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"served_share_pct","role":"measure","type":"number","label":"Residents within a 10-minute walk","unit":"%","aggregation":"none"},{"id":"offices","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Offices","unit":"offices","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"offices_beyond_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Offices beyond a 10-minute walk","unit":"offices","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"schools_beyond_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Schools beyond a 10-minute walk","unit":"schools","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"hospitals_beyond_10min","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Hospitals beyond a 10-minute walk","unit":"hospitals","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"area_km2","role":"measure","type":"number","label":"Area","unit":"km²","aggregation":"sum"},{"id":"density_per_km2","role":"measure","type":"integer","label":"Population density","unit":"people per km²